course: dictionary
lesson: 9346
title: Many meanings of spit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The sentence around it tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Brush twice a day, then spit but do not rinse.» Spit here is about your mouth and toothpaste, so it means to push liquid out of your mouth.
explain: «Breath smells in the morning because germs grow in the mouth overnight when there is less spit.» Here spit is a thing, not an action. Try the meaning in the sentence: less liquid in the mouth makes sense, so spit means the liquid in your mouth.
explain: «Llamas spit when annoyed, mostly at other llamas.» Spit is something the llamas do, so here it is a verb. Ask yourself: is the word a thing or an action? A spitting image is different again: it means someone looks exactly like another person.
fact: Spit means the liquid in your mouth, which is called saliva.
fact: As a verb, to spit means to push liquid or food out of your mouth.
fact: A spit is a long metal rod for roasting meat over a fire, and it is also a long, narrow point of land going out into the sea.
fact: Spitting can describe light rain, as in «It's spitting outside, so take a coat.»
fact: To be the spitting image of someone means you look exactly like them.
exercise: «Brush twice a day, then spit but do not rinse, so the fluoride stays on the teeth.» What does spit mean here? | Light rain | A long metal rod for cooking | *To push liquid out of your mouth | A point of land going out into the sea
exercise: «Breath smells in the morning because germs grow in the mouth overnight when there is less spit.» What is spit in this sentence? | To push food out of your mouth | A long, narrow point of land | Light rain | *The liquid in your mouth
exercise: «Llamas spit when annoyed, mostly at other llamas.» What does spit mean? | Look exactly like someone | Cook meat over a fire | Fall as light rain | *To push liquid out of the mouth at someone
test: «Some swiftlets build nests almost entirely from their own hardened spit.» What is spit in this sentence? | A drop of rain | *Liquid from the mouth, called saliva | To push food out of the mouth | A long metal rod for roasting meat
test: In geography, what is a spit? | A metal rod for roasting meat | *A long, narrow point of land going out into the sea | A bird's nest made from spit | A drop of light rain
exam: Which phrase means someone looks exactly like another person? | It's spitting | Spit toothpaste | Spit it out | *Spitting image
